["<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Whitehill v. Elkins, President, University of Maryland, et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/45ae4882-5bb6-413d-8482-85d4b2a2ed4f.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nReverse - old oath is\nunconstitutional so that is it -\n\nElbrandt case on legislative gloss --\nAG cannot change oath every time\nit is attacked.\n\nHarlan, J.\nAff -\nNothing but reference to Section 13\nnothing else -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>International Longshoremen&#x27;s Association, Local 1291 v. Philadelphia Marine Trade Association</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/00c6b931-26bf-4d1f-81e4-2738062ed69d.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nSinclair controls -\nFor the petitioner --\n\nIf Ct gave every remedy what would we\ndo\nQuestion is one of injunction\n\nBlack, J.\nagree\n\nHarlan, J.\nWilling to listen to Brennan -\nThink Sinclair controls this one -\nPrepared to make it five\nto reverse Sinclair -\n\n65D was not satisfied in this\n[struck: tools] case</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>International Longshoremen&#x27;s Association, Local 1291 v. Philadelphia Marine Trade Association</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/cf8bca92-2205-4f6a-adc8-7d063b561bfd.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J.\nSinclair was wrong\nReverse on 65D - lack of\ncustom by trial court.\n\nWhite, J.\nR on 65D\n\n[struck: Marshall] [inserted: Brennan], J.\nStick with his dissent —</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Ginsberg v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b92c9c58-f82b-4af4-a0d2-36584ea4ad58.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nAffirm\n\nBlack, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nDouglas, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nHarlan, J.\nAffirm subject to mootness</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Perma Life Mufflers, Inc., et al. v. International Parts Corp. et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/aaa9eac8-4da9-4db5-a461-9f7ad0782f43.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Affirm]\nClose case — not sure it would\ninterfere with [underlined: Simpson] and other cases\n\nBlack, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nDouglas, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nSimpson can be distinguished — never\nthought anything about pari-delicto\n//\n\nHarlan, J.\n[underlined: Affirm]\nCan not hold pari delicto is not\nvalid —\nIn this case -- it clearly\napplies —</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Perma Life Mufflers, Inc., et al. v. International Parts Corp. et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/c0878ac3-071d-442a-8206-755f41828a93.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\n[underlined: Affirm]\nleans to affirmance -- applies\nbreach of contract and other cases —\n— There are bad boys\n\nStewart, J.\nsee his dissent in Simpson —\n\nFortas, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nPari-delicto is old horse — worn out\n=\ndifficult to see who would not be\nguilty in treble damage suit —\n=\nexclusionary rule --</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>First Agricultural National Bank of Berkshire County v. State Tax Commission</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2cbb6829-f94e-4946-be07-09d23e33da71.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Reverse]\nNational Banks no longer\ninstrument of the government -\nCongress having taken over the\nfunction - we have to follow\nthat\n\nDouglas, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n[inserted: However,]\nCannot agree National Banks\nno longer instrument of government\n\nHarlan, J.\n[underlined: Affirm]\nDifferent from the\ngood old days</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>First Agricultural National Bank of Berkshire County v. State Tax Commission</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/7c3ab9ef-c25b-4762-b9fc-81f5626d36ec.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nOn chief&#x27;s grounds</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Rabeck v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/df3111f1-d1f7-4d4b-8d1a-8cb209346a2a.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Reversed]\nBd has right to hear this without going\nthrough all of the union procedure – -\nRegional office refused to hear charges –\n\nBlack, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nDouglas, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nHarlan, J.\n[underlined: Affirm]\nHastie&#x27;s opinion</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Rabeck v. New York</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/085ec484-3dbc-464f-9d4a-be0fcd6862d8.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\nReverse\nNot for interest of union or employer -\nthis is for the benefit of the union -\n= See history in Allis Chalmers -\n=\n\nStewart, J.\nAffirm\n\nWhite, J.\nAffirm\n\nFortas, J.\nReverse\nDo not think provision applies\nin case of a dismissal of ?</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>American Commercial Lines, Inc., et al. v. Louisville &amp; Nashville Railroad Co. et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/95d7b381-e21f-47cd-ba38-f927ac394b4c.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Reverse]\nLeft to the I.C.C. - up to them to fix\nrates, etc - Justified in their finding -- they\nshould consider the [underlined: full] costs -\n\nJob for I.C.C. and they acted quite\ncorrectly - -\n\nBlack, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nDouglas, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nHarlan, J.\nAffirm\nIssue is which carrier had the\ninherent advantage\n=\nCt. held correctly -- on remand the\nCommission could use the new test -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>American Commercial Lines, Inc., et al. v. Louisville &amp; Nashville Railroad Co. et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/10ac9958-8cb7-4de0-80e0-8b41c73b1169.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\nReverse\n\nStewart, J.\nAffirm\n\nWhite, J.\nReverse\n\nFortas, J.\nReverse</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Harrison v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/fda57098-1b9f-419c-ba51-f46da7e5fa35.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[inserted: Affirm]\nThis is not Simmons --\n\nBlack, J.\nAffirm\n\nDouglas, J.\nReverse\nTraynor in Cort case\n\nHarlan, J.\nAffirm\n\nNo speedy trial</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Harrison v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/7f291bb7-3d64-4ac5-82a6-07edfd679406.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\n[underlined: Reverse] on Wong Sun\n\nStewart, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nEvidence could be used\nis good rule -- would not\nhave testified because of\nconfessions</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Sabbath v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/3cd3f01e-3247-4e32-9bbf-97587cc8c973.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Reverse]\nUnlocked house entitled to same\ntype of protection as a securely locked\nhouse -\n=\nno probable cause - -\n\n//\n\nBlack, J.\nAffirm\n\nDouglas, J.\nRev\n\nHarlan, J.\n[underlined: Affirm]\nnot a statutory problem - statute\nwas for serving a search warrant +,\n(Miller case - - Ker case -)</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Sabbath v. United States</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/cabf228d-d2c8-4b8f-b7fe-0c8ff4c01e87.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\nStatutory case — Exceptions\nemergency, etc\n\nStewart, J.\n[underlined: Reverse:]\nStatute is binding —\nnothing to do with\nprobable cause\n\nWhite, J.\n[underlined: Reverse]\n\nFortas, J.\nReverse</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>King, Commissioner, Department of Pensions and Security, et al. v. Smith et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/f26fe86a-709d-4a8d-aad5-1350081ddaae.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nAffirm\nStrike it down --\nnot Due Process or Equal Protection -\nWould go on the statute solely\nnothing else other than Supremacy\nClause -\n\nDouglas, J.\nAffirm\nEqual protection clause -\n\nHarlan, J.\nAffirm\ngo on the statute -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>King, Commissioner, Department of Pensions and Security, et al. v. Smith et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/4794097c-74c3-4327-a038-bc1c0262fd4b.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Brennan, J.\n[underlined: Affirm]\n[underlined: Statute] - not Supremacy Clause - -\n\nStewart, J.\nAffirm\n[underlined: Statute]\n\nWhite, J.\n[underlined: Statute]\n\nFortas, J.\n[underlined: statute]</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Hughes v. Washington</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/beba6f18-54cc-4698-bed4-e977a4404c55.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nFederal &amp; not state law applies\na federal patentee under our cases\nholds vested right to accretions\nat the shore. Although did not\nbring with it application of\nstate law. Patentee takes\naccreted land to-day of buys\nfrom govt &amp; can&#x27;t have in\ncongruous situation of law\ndepending upon when its ac-\nquired. Rev to pac\n\nBlack, J. If instead of added to it was\ntaken from, the loser would be\nthe owner. Can&#x27;t see why when\nadded to it doesn&#x27;t go to him\nCould say its federal law because\nfederal control marginal sea</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Hughes v. Washington</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/b224dd20-7298-4eb3-96d7-6838f55bb9f4.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:4000/6000\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. Landowner got the land plus\nthe accretions or minus the\nerosion. So it was before\nstatehood. Dont think can\nchange rules of game without\ncompensating for it\n\nWhite, J.\nNot only what law governs\nreading of patent but also\nQuestion of what power\nstate had to change existing\nrules of accretions must be\ndecided.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Lee et al. v. Florida</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/43d56da2-6490-40fb-beba-8d140a71dd96.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1856\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice This is wiretapping\nviolating § 605 &amp; Sd\noverrule Schwartz v Texas</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Federal Trade Commission v. Fred Meyer, Inc., et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/9a02a4b9-374d-4f1b-aca1-5f7720b38e0c.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1939\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre><span class=\"wait\">No writing on this page.</span></pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term</p><h2>Barber v. Page, Warden</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/f3555fd1-e513-4b04-afe1-5eb910c6aacd.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1500/1961\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\nTurn this only on facts\nof this case - the deal the\nprosecutors made to let\nthis fellow off makes it\nconduct unconscionable</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Witherspoon v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/7d721483-a8c9-4eaf-8522-e090a1684fd4.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1587/1746\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>The Chief Justice\n[underlined: Reverse]\n(a) On basis of Illinois statute -- way it\nwas worded -\n(b) The way the judge handled the\ncase\n\nThe statute [underlined: plus] the way it\nwas administered makes it bad\n\nBumper just the opposite and would\naffirm that issue in Bumper -</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1967 term &nbsp;/&nbsp; notes taken by TMarshall</p><h2>Witherspoon v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/dbfc85a9-21e5-46d2-9e41-5624ce216db5.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1568/1231\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><p